<BaseLayout title="Korea Help — Seen in Korea" description="Practical help with Korean-language calls, bookings and everyday friction.">
  <main><section class="listing-hero dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">KOREA HELP</div><h1>WE HELP YOU<br />HANDLE IT.</h1><p>Calls, bookings, questions, price checks and practical Korean-language friction. This is the service layer—not a translation-only product.</p></div></section>
  <section><div class="wrap grid-3"><article class="mini"><span class="tag">CALL</span><div><h3>Call a Korean business</h3><p>Confirm availability, price, requirements or a simple request.</p></div></article><article class="mini"><span class="tag">BOOK</span><div><h3>Make a reservation</h3><p>Hospital, salon, restaurant or other appointment where direct help is appropriate.</p></div></article><article class="mini"><span class="tag">CHECK</span><div><h3>Clarify a charge or condition</h3><p>Ask what a fee means, what documents are needed, or why a condition applies.</p></div></article></div></section>
  <section><div class="wrap"><div class="cta"><div><div class="eyebrow">INITIAL MVP</div><h2>Start manually.<br />Automate after demand.</h2><p>Keep the first version simple. Add payments and workflow automation only after repeat demand is proven.</p></div><div class="cta-actions"><a href="mailto:hello@seeninkorea.com">EMAIL REQUEST</a></div></div></div></section></main>
